// A file read and written piece by piece: the log of `lines` (two million lines, 125 MB) is
// opened with `File.openText`, read with `readLine` into one text that is used again for
// every line, and each line is written with its number in front (`17: INFO 350 ...`) through
// a `StreamWriter` from `File.createText`, which writes in blocks of 64 KB. Each line is
// checked to be UTF-8 as it is read. `run.py` makes the log; both files are in
// `target/bench`.
Result<void, IoError> main() {
    var reader = try File.openText("target/bench/lines.in")
    var writer = try File.createText("target/bench/copy-sg.out")
    string line = ""
    long lines = 0
    while try reader.readLine(ref line) {
        lines += 1
        try writer.writeLine($"{lines}: {line}")
    }
    try writer.close()
    print($"{lines} lines copied")
    return Ok()
}
